WEBVTT

00:05.733 --> 00:08.333
Log in to the Conference Proposal Interface

00:08.333 --> 00:12.300
using your TIES-enabled ITU User Account.

00:14.566 --> 00:15.933
Select ‘My browser’

00:15.933 --> 00:18.933
on the left side of the screen.

00:19.133 --> 00:21.700
Search for the basic text.

00:21.700 --> 00:25.433
You can do this by typing a
keyword or a specific provision

00:25.433 --> 00:28.433
number into the search bar

00:29.766 --> 00:31.233
Or you can manually browse

00:31.233 --> 00:34.566
by clicking the arrows to
expand the Basic Texts tree,

00:34.900 --> 00:38.500
drilling down from Chapters
to Articles to specific sections

00:38.500 --> 00:41.833
of the Constitution, Convention or other texts.

00:44.566 --> 00:47.033
Once you locate your target provision,

00:47.033 --> 00:50.233
click the icon next to the provision to open a drop-down

00:50.233 --> 00:53.233
menu of ‘Actions’.

00:54.000 --> 00:56.100
Choose one of the standardized tags

00:56.100 --> 00:59.100
from the drop-down menu.

01:00.600 --> 01:02.300
On selecting an Action,

01:02.300 --> 01:05.733
the selected provision moves into your ‘My skeleton’ list.

01:06.366 --> 01:09.800
If you select ‘ADD’ for a new provision, CPI

01:09.833 --> 01:13.500
will automatically prompt you to give it a temporary letter or number.

01:14.100 --> 01:17.933
For example, adding provision 2A under Article 1.

01:18.600 --> 01:23.200
Use the pencil icon in your skeleton
list to modify the temporary title.

01:25.733 --> 01:26.633
Once all your

01:26.633 --> 01:29.633
provisions and actions have moved to ‘My skeleton’,

01:29.700 --> 01:33.100
click the red ‘Save my skeleton’
to generate your file.

01:34.633 --> 01:36.833
On clicking ‘Save my skeleton’,

01:36.833 --> 01:41.600
a dialogue box is displayed asking you to designate the Sources of the proposal.

01:42.233 --> 01:44.766
Choose one of the three options

01:44.766 --> 01:47.766
Submit as your individual Member State

01:48.166 --> 01:50.000
Submit as a Regional Group,

01:50.000 --> 01:51.000
for example,

01:51.000 --> 01:54.000
European common proposal

01:54.400 --> 01:58.200
Submit as a multi-country submission with co-signatories

01:59.366 --> 02:00.500
By default,

02:00.500 --> 02:03.500
the name of your Member State will be displayed.

02:03.600 --> 02:08.166
To add co-signatory countries, use the drop-down list of Member States.

02:08.933 --> 02:12.133
Add a suffix if the contribution is an addendum

02:12.133 --> 02:15.133
to an existing contribution.

02:15.833 --> 02:17.900
Click ‘Save my skeleton’ to lock

02:17.900 --> 02:20.900
in your structure and generate a word file.

02:21.366 --> 02:24.033
Since CPI is a web interface,

02:24.033 --> 02:27.733
the actual text modifications
are not saved in CPI.

02:28.600 --> 02:31.766
CPI only generates the baseline file.

02:34.033 --> 02:35.633
To retrieve a skeleton,

02:35.633 --> 02:39.200
click ‘Load previous skeleton’ at
the top of the interface.

02:41.533 --> 02:43.566
Once saved, CPI

02:43.566 --> 02:47.533
will assign a provisional number and a unique ticket name to your document.

02:48.166 --> 02:50.866
Do not modify or delete these codes

02:50.866 --> 02:53.600
as they contain hidden texts used by ITU’s

02:53.600 --> 02:55.466
internal systems to track

02:55.466 --> 02:57.100
the document’s history.

02:59.400 --> 03:00.766
The MS Word file

03:00.766 --> 03:02.500
will be emailed to the address

03:02.500 --> 03:04.866
linked to your TIES account.

03:04.866 --> 03:07.266
Open this MS Word document to view

03:07.266 --> 03:09.200
your selected provisions.

03:11.433 --> 03:12.700
The finalization

03:12.700 --> 03:15.700
and submission happen outside the web browser.

03:16.166 --> 03:17.533
Open the word file

03:17.533 --> 03:19.333
and draft your actual text.

03:19.966 --> 03:22.633
If the action selected was ‘MOD’,

03:22.633 --> 03:24.200
turn on track changes

03:24.200 --> 03:25.733
before you type your edits.

03:27.600 --> 03:30.833
Below the text is a section titled, Reasons.

03:31.566 --> 03:34.566
Use this to justify your proposal.

03:35.700 --> 03:37.000
Use the cover page

03:37.000 --> 03:38.333
generated to add an

03:38.333 --> 03:40.500
introduction section, if needed.

03:41.100 --> 03:42.733
Add a heading and paragraph

03:42.733 --> 03:44.366
introducing your document.

03:45.100 --> 03:46.166
The introduction

03:46.166 --> 03:48.166
and reasons will not be included when

03:48.166 --> 03:50.766
documents are in-sessions (DTs).

03:52.700 --> 03:54.933
Once your document is complete,

03:54.933 --> 03:57.433
save it locally on your computer.

03:58.966 --> 04:01.966
Your Administration’s Member State Focal Point

04:02.000 --> 04:05.000
must now officially submit this via email.

04:06.600 --> 04:08.833
For multicounty contributions,

04:08.833 --> 04:12.833
add the Focal Points of other Administration Member States to the email.
